# Every mutable variable with static storage in Clockwork's own code, and what
# it is. scripts/check-globals.sh holds the build to this list
# (docs/ENGINES.md.3).
#
#   class [only=platform-or-option,...] | variable | why
#
# engine    belongs to one engine; must move onto it (docs/ENGINES.md)
# bridge    one per plugin-bridge process, which serves one engine
# shared    one per process, for the reason given
# constant  built once at start-up, before anything reads it, and unable to
#           be a compile-time constant (the reason says why); or a value
#           still to be labelled constexpr or const, which then leaves the
#           list (the reason says "to be labelled").
# test      only tests write it
#
# A C or C++ variable with internal linkage is named `file.cpp: name`;
# anything else by its demangled name alone (a Rust static by its path).

# ── The engine core ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bridge | plugin_track.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_lane_base | TrackModel: where the engine's lanes are, which the bridge process is told
shared | guest_malloc.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_all_calls | the whole program's mallocs after boot: the process's, counted only on the web, where a process holds one core
shared | guest_malloc.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_all_held | the whole program's mallocs after boot: the process's, counted only on the web, where a process holds one core
shared | guest_malloc.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_host_scratch | the whole program's mallocs after boot: the process's, counted only on the web, where a process holds one core
shared | guest_malloc.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_mark_calls | the whole program's mallocs after boot: the process's, counted only on the web, where a process holds one core
shared | guest_malloc.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_mark_held | the whole program's mallocs after boot: the process's, counted only on the web, where a process holds one core

# ── Constants: built once, or to be labelled ─────────────────────────────────
constant | audio_processor.cpp: guest_info::info | the linked guest's description: dsp_describe() answers at run time, so it is read once
constant | osc::BeginArray | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::BeginBundleImmediate | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::EndArray | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::EndBundle | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::EndMessage | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::Infinitum | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::Nil | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | osc::OscNil | oscpack's tag objects: to be labelled inline constexpr (vendor/oscpack/CLOCKWORK-CHANGES.md)
constant | plugin_discovery.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::searchPaths::paths | the plugin folders, built once from the environment
constant | ClockworkEngine.cpp: ClockworkEngine::sendDeviceReport::{lambda}::operator()(osc::OutboundPacketStream&) const::canonical | to be a constexpr array
constant | plugin_vst3.cpp: clockwork_plugin_vst3::(anonymous namespace)::HostContext::getName(char16_t*)::kName | to be labelled constexpr: a writable pointer to constant text today
constant | plugin_vst3.cpp: clockwork_plugin_vst3::(anonymous namespace)::tuidToHex(char const*)::kHex | to be labelled constexpr: a writable pointer to constant text today

# ── One per process ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
shared | clockwork_core::LAST_ID | the registry of cores: the last id handed out
shared | clockwork_core::LIVE | the registry of cores: how many are live, so a process that holds one refuses a second
shared | clockwork_core::HANDLES | the registry of cores: every handle made, newest first, for the walks over the live cores
shared | clockwork_core::GUESTS | the registry of cores: how many hold a guest instance, against how many the guest says a process may hold
shared | clockwork_heap::map::MAP | the address map: which core's heap owns each chunk of memory, for a free from any thread (docs/ENGINES.md)
shared | audio_processor.cpp: pool_check_wanted::wanted | CLOCKWORK_POOL_CHECK, read once by the process: a diagnostic every core follows
shared | clockwork_heap::core_heap::OUTLIVED | cores that went with clockwork memory still in their own pool: the process's count, which the tests require at 0
shared | clockwork_heap::core_heap::OUTLIVED_FREES | frees of blocks that outlived their core, dropped and counted: the process's count, which the tests require at 0
shared | clockwork_heap::entry::ENTRY | each thread's entry: the core its call works inside and the kind of call (docs/ENGINES.md)
shared | audio_processor.cpp: t_instance_ring_of | each thread's: the core whose instance's ring it is the one writer of
shared | plugin_clap.cpp: clockwork_plugin_clap::(anonymous namespace)::g_err | each thread's last error, as errno
shared | plugin_vst3.cpp: clockwork_plugin_vst3::(anonymous namespace)::g_err | each thread's last error, as errno
shared | RingReader.cpp: tReaderOfThisThread | one per Clockwork thread, which reader runs on it; to be a std::thread::id member
shared | plugin_discovery.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_extra | per bridge process: discovery settings
shared | plugin_discovery.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_extraMu | per bridge process: discovery settings
shared | plugin_discovery.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_scan_ctx | per bridge process: discovery settings
shared | plugin_discovery.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_scan_fn | per bridge process: discovery settings
shared | plugin_clap.cpp: clockwork_plugin_clap::(anonymous namespace)::g_scan_cache | per bridge process: the scan results
shared | plugin_clap.cpp: clockwork_plugin_clap::(anonymous namespace)::g_scan_mu | per bridge process: the scan results
shared | plugin_vst3.cpp: clockwork_plugin_vst3::(anonymous namespace)::g_scan_cache | per bridge process: the scan results
shared | plugin_vst3.cpp: clockwork_plugin_vst3::(anonymous namespace)::g_scan_mu | per bridge process: the scan results
shared only=macos | PluginEditorWindow.mm: (anonymous namespace)::ensureApp::done | the bridge main thread's editor windows
shared only=macos | PluginEditorWindow.mm: (anonymous namespace)::registry::r | the bridge main thread's editor windows
shared | clockwork_audio_file.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::gDecodeLimit | the client's decode limit; to be an argument of the decode call
shared | ClockworkEngine.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_defaultDrivers | the default drivers a test installs to keep every engine off real audio
shared | ClockworkEngine.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::g_defaultDriversMutex | the default drivers a test installs to keep every engine off real audio
shared | clockwork_gamepad::ffi::GLOBAL | the gamepad poller; its events fan out to every core
shared | mem_region.cpp: clockwork::mem::(anonymous namespace)::g_arena | the memory provider over the process's memory; its first-fit allocator to be the TLSF
shared | mem_region.cpp: clockwork::mem::(anonymous namespace)::g_arena_size | the memory provider over the process's memory; its first-fit allocator to be the TLSF
shared | mem_region.cpp: clockwork::mem::(anonymous namespace)::g_arena_used | the memory provider over the process's memory; its first-fit allocator to be the TLSF
shared | mem_region.cpp: clockwork::mem::(anonymous namespace)::g_head | the memory provider over the process's memory; its first-fit allocator to be the TLSF
shared | mem_region.cpp: clockwork::mem::(anonymous namespace)::g_lock | the memory provider over the process's memory; its first-fit allocator to be the TLSF
shared | clockwork_midi::device::SHARED | the MIDI service's device IO, for the sinks that send through it
shared | clockwork_midi::ffi::PROCESS | the MIDI service: one OS client, a handle per core, closed by the last
shared | ClockworkEngine.cpp: (anonymous namespace)::publishedAppName::name | the name the OS shows; to be set once by the process, not by every engine's boot
shared | clockwork_log::SINK | the one log sink; a line names its core
shared | clockwork_sinks::service::DRAIN | the one sink drain thread, which walks every core's sinks
shared | clockwork_sinks::service::RUNNING | the one sink drain thread, which walks every core's sinks
shared | clockwork_sinks::service::TABLES | the one sink drain thread's list of every core's table
shared | plugin_vst3.cpp: clockwork_plugin_vst3::(anonymous namespace)::hostContext::ctx | the one stateless IHostApplication every plugin in the bridge is handed
shared only=windows | clockwork_midi::watcher::MTA | the Windows COM apartment, an OS fact of the process

# ── Tests only ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
test | clockwork_log::capture::SEEN | only tests read it; to go behind a feature only they turn on
test | rt_alloc::g_in_rt | only the test binary's operator new reads it; to be the thread's Entry

